# ALU Ventures web client — environment variables.
#
# The client needs NO environment variables. In development Vite proxies /api
# to the local API (client/vite.config.js); in production Vercel rewrites
# /api/* to the Render API (client/vercel.json). Never put secrets here: any
# VITE_* value would be visible to every visitor.
#
# Optional, development only: API_PROXY changes where `npm run dev` proxies
# /api (default http://localhost:4000). vite.config.js reads it from the shell,
# not from a .env file, for example:
#   macOS / Linux / Git Bash:  API_PROXY=http://localhost:4001 npm run dev
#   Windows PowerShell:        $env:API_PROXY="http://localhost:4001"; npm run dev
API_PROXY=http://localhost:4000
